.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt PMM_ALLOC 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm pmm_alloc_block ,
.Nm pmm_alloc_contiguous
.Nd allocate physical memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/pmm.h
.Ft "void *"
.Fn pmm_alloc_block "void"
.Ft "void *"
.Fn pmm_alloc_contiguous "size_t count"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pmm_alloc_block
function allocates a single page of physical memory.
.Pp
The
.Fn pmm_alloc_contiguous
function allocates
.Fa count
contiguous pages of physical memory.
.Pp
Note that these functions return
.emph virtual addresses
in the kernel direct map region (0xC0000000+), not raw physical addresses.
To use these addresses with hardware that requires physical addresses (e.g. paging structures, DMA), you must subtract 0xC0000000 or use
.Fn pmap_extract .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn pmm_alloc_block
and
.Fn pmm_alloc_contiguous
functions return a kernel virtual address pointing to the allocated memory, or
.Dv NULL
if the allocation failed (Out of Memory).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pmm_free_block 9 ,
.Xr pmm_free_contiguous 9 ,
.Xr pmap 9
.Sh HISTORY
The PMM allocator first appeared in Substrate.
